-- title:
--   Finite local inputs for retained atlas tiles
-- statement:
--   For anisotropic lattice scales $L$ and a fixed rectangular cell $R$, a finite set of lattice parents contains every parent capable of producing $R$. This candidate set is the input to the locality argument for retained tiles. It permits tile membership to be determined from finitely many marker and cut decisions near the fixed rectangle.
-- source:
